        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/69888?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">reduced the occurrence of easy and easier within the CSS guides section.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42324",
            "title": "Remove EASY from CSS guides section",
            "date_modified": "2025-12-09T16:39:52.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-12-09T16:38:21.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "estelle",
                "url": "https://github.com/estelle"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/939727?u=2e25f47c213a7e8f2e4e57ddd4ee59ba6601eae3&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Adds brief summaries of <code class=\"notranslate\">referenceTarget</code> on <code class=\"notranslate\">attachShadow()</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">ShadowRoot</code>, and <code class=\"notranslate\">shadowrootreferencetarget</code> on <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;template&gt;</code>.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Implemented experimentally in Chrome and positive signals from Mozilla and funding to implement in WebKit as well as progress in the HTML and WHATNOT arenas.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Explainer: <a href=\"https://github.com/WICG/webcomponents/blob/gh-pages/proposals/reference-target-explainer.md\">https://github.com/WICG/webcomponents/blob/gh-pages/proposals/reference-target-explainer.md</a></li>\n<li>HTML progress: <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2592669740\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/10707\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/whatwg/html/issues/10707/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/10707\">whatwg/html#10707</a></li>\n<li>WHATNOT progress: <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3403461116\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/11648\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/whatwg/html/issues/11648/hovercard?comment_id=3293932780&amp;comment_type=issue_comment\" href=\"https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/11648#issuecomment-3293932780\">whatwg/html#11648 (comment)</a></li>\n<li>Chrome implementation status: <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5188237101891584\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5188237101891584</a></li>\n<li>Positive signal from Mozilla: <a href=\"https://mozilla.github.io/standards-positions/#1035\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://mozilla.github.io/standards-positions/#1035</a></li>\n<li>Plans for WebKit implementation: <a href=\"https://blogs.igalia.com/mrego/solving-cross-root-aria-issues-in-shadow-dom/\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://blogs.igalia.com/mrego/solving-cross-root-aria-issues-in-shadow-dom/</a></li>\n</ul>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42323",
            "title": "Add shadow root reference target information",
            "date_modified": "2025-12-09T16:28:06.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-12-09T16:24:45.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "meyerweb",
                "url": "https://github.com/meyerweb"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/69888?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">Removed most occurrences of the word \"easy\" from the glossary pages.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42322",
            "title": "Remove EASY from glossary",
            "date_modified": "2025-12-09T16:05:30.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-12-09T16:03:49.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "estelle",
                "url": "https://github.com/estelle"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">In Firefox 147, when pseudo-element nodes are selected in the HTML pane of the Inspector — for example, those representing generated content created by <code class=\"notranslate\">::before</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">::after</code> rules — you can now edit the selectors of the corresponding rules in the Rule view. See <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1998704\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1998704</a>.</p>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42316",
            "title": "Fx147 devtools edit pseudo element selector",
            "date_modified": "2025-12-09T14:39:03.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-12-09T14:37:30.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">FF147 supports brotli compression in <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/CompressionStream/CompressionStream\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">CompressionStream</code> constructor</a> and <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/DecompressionStream/DecompressionStream\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">DecompressionStream()</code> constructor</a> in <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1921583\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1921583</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This adds a release note. It also updates the two constructors to include the brotli option and zstd option (which is also supported).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs work: <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3699242115\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42251\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/42251/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42251\">#42251</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42312",
            "title": "FF147 Relnote: CompressionStream/DecompressionStream support brotli +…",
            "date_modified": "2025-12-09T20:11:01.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-12-09T06:30:34.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">As discussed in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3708656574\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42306\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/42306/hovercard?comment_id=3629944371&amp;comment_type=issue_comment\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42306#issuecomment-3629944371\">#42306 (comment)</a> the description of import assertions does not provide an easy way to link to particular parts of the concepts, such as a definition of CSS Modules imported using <code class=\"notranslate\">with { type: \"css\"}</code>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This restructures the existing material to provide some headings. Should allow clean linking to the doc, easier parsing for readers, and maintenance if we later add other module types.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/Josh-Cena/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/Josh-Cena\">@Josh-Cena</a> Obviously \"for discussion and iteration\". It is almost all a restructure, with only a tiny amount of new content, which I will highlight.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs work being done in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3699248949\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42255\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/42255/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42255\">#42255</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42309",
            "title": "Restructure import assertions description to ease maintainability",
            "date_modified": "2025-12-09T16:21:52.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-12-09T05:26:55.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">FF147 adds support for module scripts in <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1986681\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1986681</a>. This allows you to do stuff like below to import a stylesheet and adopt it into your document.</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-js notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"import sheet from './styles.css' with { type: 'css' };\ndocument.adoptedStyleSheets = [sheet];\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-k\">import</span> <span class=\"pl-s1\">sheet</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">from</span> <span class=\"pl-s\">'./styles.css'</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">with</span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">{</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">type</span>: <span class=\"pl-s\">'css'</span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">}</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">;</span>\n<span class=\"pl-smi\">document</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">.</span><span class=\"pl-c1\">adoptedStyleSheets</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">[</span><span class=\"pl-s1\">sheet</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">]</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">;</span></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This adds a release note.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3699248949\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42255\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/42255/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42255\">#42255</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42306",
            "title": "FF147 Relnote: CSS Module scripts",
            "date_modified": "2025-12-09T02:36:08.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-12-09T00:59:23.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        }
    ]
